inflateSync: file-scope selectany mark[]

Kind: link-layout stand-in, as 0003.

The reference holds inflateSync's static mark[4] = {0, 0, 0xff, 0xff}
right after border[] (infblock.obj). A block-scope static is ordinary .rdata
in inflate.obj and cannot be ordered; stock source moves 4709 bytes. The
file-scope selectany object is ordered after border and kept by
layout/server.dll/game-includes.rsp.

--- a/inflate.c
+++ b/inflate.c
@@ -301,6 +301,13 @@
 }
 
 
+/* inflateSync's marker bytes, moved out of block scope into a selectany
+ * object so common-data-order.txt can place them right after border[], where
+ * the original image has them (the static's object-order position).
+ * layout/server.dll/game-includes.rsp keeps the COMDAT that /OPT:REF would
+ * drop with inflateSync, as the static's plain .rdata was kept. */
+__declspec(selectany) const Byte mark[4] = {0, 0, 0xff, 0xff};
+
 int ZEXPORT inflateSync(z)
 z_streamp z;
 {
@@ -325,7 +332,6 @@
